WEBVTT

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.620
The battle between Akagi and 
Urabe has finally begun.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.660
Akagi has unleashed an attack 
that alarms his opponent.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.220
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.220
<b>The Magic of Coincidence</b>

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.990
<i>What's with this kid?</i>

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.960
<i>A multi-sided wait for a suu ankou?!</i>

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.000
<i>After he declared an open riichi,</i>

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.470
<i>I dealt into his hand with 
this 2 of characters.</i>

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.050
<i>It's mangan hand and 
he's going to let it go?</i>

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.980
<i>So he's dead set on drawing the 
tile he needs for the suu ankou?</i>

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:48.250
<i>If he really believes that 
will happen, he's just trash.</i>

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.990
<i>Your sense of gambling is weak!</i>

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.420
<i>If you can't do it,</i>

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.530
<i>you will have missed the 
opportunity to get a</i>

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:00.030
<i>direct mangan hit off of me for good.</i>

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:05.030
<i>The last straws of victory will 
be slipping from your grasp here!</i>

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.290
<i>Damn, breaking my hand to deal 
into his has made my draws crap.</i>

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.510
<i>This time he passed on a tsumo win.</i>

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.450
<i>He insists on going for the suu ankou.</i>

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.750
<i>He's crazy.</i>

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:25.310
<i>There it is.</i>

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.650
<i>I'm back in tenpai.</i>

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.220
<i>A double pon wait for 6 
and 8 of characters.</i>

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.930
<i>I'll make you regret your 
ridiculous play style.</i>

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.560
And in the 15th turn,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.830
Akagi draws yet another winning tile.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.350
<i>There it is.</i>

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:42.670
<i>He can't draw it out any longer.</i>

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.170
<i>There are only two draws left.</i>

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.930
<i>Besides, he can't discard 
this tile against Urabe.</i>

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.450
<i>Urabe has a chinitsu hand... 
He can't be waiting for anything else.</i>

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.630
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:01.700
<i>This is how the top player 
of the Kawada Group</i>

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:05.020
<i>plays in a match with several 
million riding on it?</i>

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:10.030
<i>He's playing like a drunkard, 
with no sense of judgment left.</i>

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.770
Ron, chinitsu, mangan. That's 12,000!

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.040
<i>This is worst that could happen.</i>

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.170
<i>Urabe and Akagi are now 
over 70,000 points apart.</i>

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.810
<i>It's hopeless.</i>

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.040
<i>Akagi...</i>

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.980
Only two hands left...

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.020
What's wrong?

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.390
You made a mistake.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.840
You were off by one.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.230
You split it at 12.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:40.860
I'm sorry!

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:41.990
Come on, man.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.170
<i>He's calm.</i>

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:49.060
<i>Despite being in this hopeless situation.</i>

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.770
<i>Does he really have 
something in the works?</i>

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.010
<i>A secret plan to cause an upset?</i>

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.990
Akagi's starting hand.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.480
<i>Damn.</i>

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.050
<i>He gets this hand when 
we need something huge?</i>

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.320
<i>What is this?</i>

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.980
<i>His hand is getting cheaper and cheaper.</i>

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.220
<i>He's in tenpai.</i>

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.730
<i>But there's no point in 
winning with this hand.</i>

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:16.720
Kan.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.200
<i>What?</i>

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.130
<i>His trash hand suddenly 
turned into a big one.</i>

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.440
<i>Four dora, riichi, tsumo. 
That's a haneman.</i>

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.670
<i>There's no way he won't get a 
tsumo with this three-way wait.</i>

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:32.910
Riichi.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.870
<i>No way!</i>

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.060
<i>Why did he throw away 
the three-way wait?!</i>

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.180
<i>Why?!</i>

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:43.100
<i>Is it to get a direct hit off Urabe?</i>

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.660
<i>Still, that's no reason to 
throw away a three-way wait</i>

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.850
<i>for a single wait on the north wind!</i>

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.670
<i>What's more, there are already 
two out in the discards.</i>

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.160
<i>It's a hell wait.</i>

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.850
<i>Urabe is not that careless.</i>

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.920
<i>He won't discard it, no matter if it's the 
north wind or the 5, 8, or 7 of bamboo.</i>

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.080
<i>Since it won't come from him,</i>

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.410
<i>Akagi should have stayed with 
the easy three-way wait.</i>

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.640
<i>And yet he...</i>

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.140
<i>Wait.</i>

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:13.650
<i>The tile we saw in the 
beginning was a north wind.</i>

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:18.190
<i>So between the dead wall and the 
discards, that's 3 north winds out.</i>

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.940
<i>Meaning this wait is dead.</i>

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.420
<i>There's no way for him to win.</i>

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.460
<i>How could he have made such a 
mistake at this crucial moment?</i>

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.940
<i>No, Akagi would never make such 
an elementary mistake here.</i>

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.940
<i>He must have some sort of plan for this.</i>

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:40.870
<i>One possibility is that the next dead 
wall draw will be the north wind,</i>

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:44.410
<i>and that Akagi gets the 
last 6 of bamboo for a kan.</i>

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.950
<i>He'll win by drawing the north 
wind from the dead wall.</i>

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.770
<i>But the fourth 6 of bamboo 
is already in the discards.</i>

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.960
<i>So this won't happen.</i>

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.490
<i>The only possibility remaining</i>

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.460
<i>is that someone declares kan 
and discards the north wind.</i>

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:02.460
<i>But obviously, neither Urabe nor 
the other players will declare kan.</i>

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.630
<i>Nobody would willingly add more dora.</i>

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.470
<i>It's impossible.</i>

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.560
<i>There's no chance.</i>

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.240
<i>That north wind will never be discarded.</i>

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.240
<i>Another safe tile.</i>

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.820
<i>After the riichi, Urabe has 
only discarded safe tiles.</i>

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:21.880
<i>Even if he had kept his three-way wait,</i>

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.590
<i>even if there was another 
north wind somewhere,</i>

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.680
<i>Urabe would have never 
discarded the winning tile.</i>

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.250
<i>Urabe's going to play it 100% safe.</i>

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.170
<i>An easy game of Mahjong where 
he doesn't need to think.</i>

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.000
No.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.030
In fact, Urabe was struggling.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:41.530
It only seems to be an easy 
game to the observers.

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:44.540
Urabe sees the four dora.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:48.040
Akagi's riichi is nothing but ominous.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:50.970
<i>I'm in tenpai.</i>

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.170
<i>But winning with this makes no sense.</i>

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:55.550
<i>Safe tile!</i>

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.110
<i>The guy to my left already 
discarded the 7 of characters,</i>

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:01.440
<i>so I'm safe for the next turn, too.</i>

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.810
<i>The problem is the turn after that.</i>

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:09.310
<i>The tiles are clumping up...</i>

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:10.850
<i>A typical triplet game.</i>

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.390
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.420
<i>Getting all the same tiles hurts.</i>

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.040
<i>I suppose I could declare kan and 
hope my draw gives me a safe tile,</i>

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.980
<i>but if I draw a dangerous tile,</i>

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:27.150
<i>all I would have accomplished 
is giving him more dora.</i>

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:30.490
<i>Wait a second.</i>

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.650
<i>There are only two turns 
left in this hand.</i>

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.500
<i>So this one passed.</i>

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.010
<i>Now I'm safe.</i>

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.130
<i>I've made it through.</i>

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.630
<i>With only one turn left, it's over.</i>

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:49.630
<i>Another dangerous tile...</i>

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:54.140
<i>But I have a plan for 
the 17th and final turn.</i>

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:58.870
<i>The trump card handed to me 
by coincidence in the 16th turn.</i>

00:07:58.870 --> 00:07:59.620
Kan.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:05.340
<i>This tile hasn't been discarded yet.</i>

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.850
<i>Then another.</i>

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.080
Kan!

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.320
<i>Wh-What is this?</i>

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:11.450
<i>This one!</i>

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.820
<i>This is what I wanted.</i>

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.730
<i>This is the tile everybody 
saw at the beginning</i>

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.360
<i>of this hand because of that mistake.</i>

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.240
<i>I'm sure Akagi remembers that, too.</i>

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:25.070
<i>There's no way he's 
waiting for the north wind.</i>

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:30.070
<i>And with these two kan, 
he doesn't get to draw anymore.</i>

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.270
<i>I killed two birds with one stone.</i>

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.030
<i>Impossible.</i>

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:42.020
<i>Am I dreaming?</i>

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.590
You are like a secure vault right now.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.060
Any sort of half-baked attempts 
won't let me get points from that vault.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:55.840
Logic won't work.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:58.910
Logic won't even get into the keyhole.

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:04.000
In order to get the key in, 
I have to use another force.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.510
If I had to name it, I'd call 
it the force of coincidence.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.740
You can't defend against something 
that happens by accident.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.250
The key will turn with 
the help of coincidence.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:16.430
<i>It was all taken into account...</i>

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:18.600
<i>Urabe's ironclad defense,</i>

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:19.250
<i>his logic...</i>

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.580
<i>By Akagi's Mahjong which 
incorporates coincidence.</i>

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.760
<i>By his peerless capacity.</i>

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.260
I guess it's a total of 10 reverse dora.

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:31.260
With the riichi, it's a sanbaiman.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.760
<i>Two coincidences.</i>

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.850
<i>The accidental uncovering of the north wind 
at the beginning, and Urabe's two kan.</i>

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:42.770
<i>So Akagi wasn't waiting so 
much for the north wind,</i>

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.530
<i>but for the kan that would be born</i>

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:47.640
<i>from the tendency of Urabe's 
hand to yield all those triplets.</i>

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.030
<i>In other words,</i>

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.280
<i>he was waiting on the opportunity 
created by coincidence.</i>

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.340
People can evade logic,

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.330
but can't do the same with coincidence.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:59.700
A strategy that far surpasses the 
imagination of the average mind.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.340
In fact, maybe it should be called godly?

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:05.710
A blade from another realm...

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:08.870
Akagi's riichi, with a wait on coincidence.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.480
Akagi versus Urabe.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:18.840
The difference between them has 
shrunk from over 70,000 to 22,500.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:21.330
Akagi is the dealer for the last hand.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:25.080
If he gets a direct mangan hit off
of Urabe, he'll take over the lead.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.090
Urabe.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.010
Can you do this?

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:31.590
Don't worry.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:35.090
That sort of ridiculous 
win was a one-time thing.

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:37.800
I won't deal into his hand anymore.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:42.160
He won't take over the lead even 
if he gets a mangan tsumo win.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:48.810
Basically, he won't be able 
to beat me with just one hand.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.560
He won't be able to 
kill me with one arrow.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.810
He'll need a second one.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:59.530
If he only gets 3,900 or 5,800 hands, 
he'll need a third or fourth arrow.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.720
In contrast, I can win with anything.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.120
All I have to do is focus on speed,

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:11.060
while he has to worry 
about composition, as well.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:15.550
This will make all the difference 
in a short finale like this.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:16.580
Okay.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:19.580
Don't worry, Boss.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.460
He'll fall one step short.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.040
I will keep my lead.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:27.450
All right, if you say so, 
my mind is at ease.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.070
I won't say anything else.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:30.010
I'm counting on you.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.420
Yes, sir.

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.300
<i>Damn kid.</i>

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:38.490
<i>I won't let everything go your way.</i>

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.920
It's the final hand.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.960
Just you watch, I'm going 
to make my getaway.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:47.440
<i>Not bad.</i>

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.930
<i>I'm lucky.</i>

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:52.860
<i>I just need to be fast.</i>

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.310
<i>I'm going to take the shortest route, 
faster than anyone else.</i>

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.010
<i>I'm in tenpai.</i>

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:04.040
<i>An ideal tanyao, pinfu, with 
a 2 or 5 of circles wait.</i>

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:09.020
<i>Looks like luck's on my side.</i>

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:10.970
<i>Now spit it out.</i>

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:15.490
<i>I'll teach you that winning 
doesn't require these flashy plays!</i>

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:18.390
<i>A real pro always wins quietly.</i>

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:19.890
Kan.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.190
<i>What?</i>

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:25.490
<i>The 6 of bamboo?</i>

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:27.250
<i>So he has four dora?</i>

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:31.570
<i>How can his luck carry on this long?</i>

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:34.010
<i>Did he switch the tile?</i>

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:37.300
<i>No, he flipped it with just his index finger.</i>

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.590
<i>That can't be it.</i>

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:43.150
<i>His luck is immeasurable.</i>

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.960
<i>I won't need a second arrow.</i>

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:48.890
<i>I will finish you with the first.</i>

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.480
<i>Four dora... That's a guaranteed 
dealer mangan if he wins.</i>

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:55.630
<i>The moment I deal into his 
hand, my lead will disappear.</i>

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:57.900
<i>Even if I avoid a direct hit,</i>

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.540
<i>a haneman tsumo will also cause an upset.</i>

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:01.130
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:03.960
<i>Why did I have to get this tile?</i>

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.830
<i>He's probably going for a tanyao,</i>

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:09.140
<i>but it's equally likely that 
he's going for honor tiles.</i>

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.700
<i>East wind, south wind, 
and the green dragon</i>

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.530
<i>all have two tiles out 
in the discards already.</i>

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:15.150
<i>That only leaves the white and red dragon.</i>

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:18.220
<i>I just can't discard this tile.</i>

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.720
But on the next turn...

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:24.510
<i>What?</i>

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.220
<i>The red dragon passes?</i>

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:27.680
<i>That's a relief.</i>

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.600
<i>If I draw a non-terminal number tile here, 
my hand will be revived in one turn.</i>

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.940
<i>Of all things, a white dragon?</i>

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.730
<i>My luck is terrible.</i>

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.790
Again, Urabe has a single 
wait for the white dragon

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.040
where he can only win with a tsumo.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.560
<i>It makes more sense to assume</i>

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:45.700
<i>he has the first dora, 
the 6 of characters, in his hand, too.</i>

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:50.050
<i>That means tanyao or an honor tile hand 
plus five dora will give him a haneman.</i>

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.280
<i>I'll lose, even if he doesn't win off me.</i>

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.600
At this point, Urabe was 
still on the offensive.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.300
In this situation, not doing so 
would be out of the question.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:01.490
Chi!

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:03.790
Akagi makes a move on the eighth turn.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.540
<i>He discarded a dora?</i>

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:09.520
<i>Then it's certain.</i>

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.300
<i>He's in tenpai.</i>

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:12.480
<i>But is it a tanyao hand?</i>

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:13.650
<i>Or honor tiles?</i>

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:16.810
Seeing Akagi discard a 6 of characters, 
the next player follows suit.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:20.560
<i>That's the third.</i>

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:24.570
<i>Including the one in my hand, 
that's three dora tiles out.</i>

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.050
<i>The last one must be in his hand.</i>

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:28.370
<i>Damn...</i>

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:29.650
<i>What?</i>

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:31.650
<i>The fourth...</i>

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:34.810
<i>Now I know where all the dora are.</i>

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.890
<i>So that means he discarded the 
only dora that he had in his hand.</i>

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.760
<i>I thought he would take advantage of 
this situation and come in for the kill.</i>

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:47.140
<i>But I guess he's only after 
a mangan hand for now.</i>

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:53.380
<i>So even this kid gets complacent.</i>

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:58.550
And in the ninth turn, 
Urabe is at a crossroads.

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:02.060
<i>In order to maintain my tenpai,</i>

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:03.820
<i>I have to discard the 8 of bamboo 
or the white dragon.</i>

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.510
<i>The white dragon is the 
last remaining honor tile.</i>

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:10.320
<i>Yet this 8 of bamboo isn't 
exactly safe, either.</i>

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.930
<i>I don't need to overextend myself here.</i>

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.020
<i>The haneman threat is gone now.</i>

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:17.360
<i>The only danger is a direct mangan hit.</i>

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:20.330
<i>And his luck is waning, as well.</i>

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.760
<i>His call on the 2 of characters proved that.</i>

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:30.400
<i>If he still had luck, 
he should have won with that 2.</i>

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:33.420
<i>Alternatively, a 5 of characters 
would have been discarded,</i>

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.580
<i>and he could've kept his dora.</i>

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:37.350
<i>But he had no choice but to discard it.</i>

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:40.350
<i>It's a typical example of someone 
whose hand is going downhill.</i>

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:44.800
<i>He must have discarded it 
because he saw the same signs.</i>

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:46.360
<i>I'm sure of it.</i>

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:49.390
<i>Under these conditions, if I was 
bold and dealt into his hand,</i>

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:51.960
<i>I'd never be able to look 
myself in the eye anymore.</i>

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.810
<i>In any case, there's a 
certain way for me to win.</i>

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.950
<i>He won't have a chance because</i>

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.540
<i>I can crush any chance for him 
to get a mangan hit off me.</i>

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:02.210
<i>Completely!</i>

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:07.210
<i>Sorry, but I'm out.</i>

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:10.720
<i>I'm going to fight you in the next 
game since you're going downhill.</i>

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.400
<i>Akagi...</i>

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:16.730
This 4 of circles is a 
crossroads, quite literally.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:21.560
After this tile, 
Urabe's game is no longer offensive.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:23.580
He only deals safe tiles.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:24.360
He runs.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:29.460
And as if to push him even 
further, in the 13th turn...

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:33.330
<i>There it is, the white dragon.</i>

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.800
<i>That's the third.</i>

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.170
<i>The possibility of him 
having honor tiles is gone.</i>

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:40.210
<i>It's almost settled that he 
is going for a tanyao hand.</i>

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:45.780
<i>This means I can now discard the 
terminal and honor tiles I held onto</i>

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:48.240
<i>thinking he was after honor tiles.</i>

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:51.960
<i>I think I've made it.</i>

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.790
<i>Yes, I have.</i>

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.960
<i>I only have three draws left.</i>

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:00.740
<i>Even if I am forced to draw more often,</i>

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:03.140
<i>I can get out of it with safe tiles
and the terminal and honor tiles.</i>

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.010
<i>I made a clean getaway.</i>

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.040
Akagi.

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:09.920
It's fine, Ishikawa-san.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.640
The outcome of the game is not yet set.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:14.880
<i>Urabe...</i>

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:18.880
<i>Sorry, but it's too early to 
think you've gotten away.</i>

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.150
<i>I can still catch up to you.</i>

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.650
<i>Just watch, I'll make you 
freeze in your tracks.</i>

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:28.660
Urabe drew a 4 of characters, a tile 
that hasn't gotten past Akagi yet.

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:30.930
<i>No problem.</i>

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:33.320
<i>I've got two safe tiles, 
for these two turns.</i>

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:36.170
<i>Then I can use a terminal 
or honor for the last turn.</i>

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:40.710
<i>He's probably out of wacky ideas, too.</i>

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:41.900
<i>I've gotten away.</i>

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.150
It might have looked like Akagi 
had exhausted his options.

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:48.370
At least, it seemed like there 
was no chance of the game ending

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:49.910
with Urabe dealing into Akagi's hand.

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.650
But on the 17th turn...

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.780
Pon.

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:58.020
Akagi revives his hand yet again.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.290
A sanshoku doukou.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.290
Sanshoku Doukou - Three triplets consisting 
of the same numbers in all three suits.

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:02.350
<i>No way.</i>

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:06.060
<i>A sanshoku doukou this late in the game?</i>

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:09.940
<i>Then he could even be 
waiting on a single tile.</i>

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.680
<i>The terminals and honors I considered 
safe are suddenly anything but!</i>

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:14.990
<i>I have no safe tiles.</i>

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:16.300
<i>Shit.</i>

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:17.770
<i>Come on, give me a safe tile!</i>

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:18.770
<i>Huh?</i>

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.030
<i>A 7 of characters?</i>

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:21.510
<i>The second?</i>

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:25.010
<i>So he has no 7 of characters 
triplet in his hand.</i>

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.780
<i>The most he could have is a double 
pon wait for the 7 and something else.</i>

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:29.440
<i>As long as I don't discard this,</i>

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.750
<i>he won't get his sanshoku 
doukou hand together.</i>

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:35.760
<i>I see.</i>

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:39.990
<i>It looks like his monster 
luck is also on the way down.</i>

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:43.890
<i>You can't touch that north wind, can you?</i>

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:47.020
<i>It doesn't matter if you have a 
tanyao or a sanshoku doukou hand.</i>

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.240
I've gotten away.

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:50.770
Are you sure?

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:54.210
It's still too early to say.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.440
Pon.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:56.480
What?

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:57.370
Pon?

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:03.950
Akagi goes into a naked wait!

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:03.950
Naked wait - A single wait with only one tile left in your hand.

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:06.530
What the hell is this?

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:09.060
<i>He has no particular hand and 
is going for a naked wait?</i>

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.190
<i>Why would anyone do this?</i>

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:17.520
<i>I see, that pon changed the draw order.</i>

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:22.820
<i>Since there's a kan, the last draw 
will be the top tile of that wall.</i>

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.440
<i>So I'll get the last draw.</i>

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:27.390
<i>He wants to ron off my last draw?</i>

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.670
<i>So that's what he was going for?</i>

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.380
<i>The honor tiles, the open tanyao,</i>

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:37.180
<i>and even the hint of a 
sanshoku doukou were all bluffs.</i>

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:41.440
<i>Are you telling me this kid 
had me dancing to his tune?!</i>

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.060
<i>This is ridiculous.</i>

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:45.130
<i>There's too much riding on chance!</i>

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.930
<i>I won't let him have his way!</i>

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.550
<i>Give me a safe tile!</i>

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:55.170
<i>If I get a safe tile, all his crazy 
calculations will have been in vain!</i>

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.400
Urabe drew a west wind.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:00.980
The west wind has not passed Akagi yet!

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.910
It's over.

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:10.410
If you had drawn a safe tile, 
you would have had a chance to win.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:14.800
If you drew a tile that hasn't 
passed yet, you're out of luck.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:18.050
It's over.

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:22.800
Ishikawa-san, please take care of the rest.

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:23.930
H-Hey!

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.430
What are we supposed 
to do without you?

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.540
It's not certain that it'll end here!

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:31.950
It will.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.670
I cast a spell on that naked wait.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.640
Out of the 14 tiles in his hand,

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:41.810
Urabe will pick that tile 
and deal into my hand.

00:20:41.810 --> 00:20:42.680
Without fail.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.760
That's all, Ishikawa-san.

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:49.180
There's no problem.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:56.540
Everybody just stared at that tile, 
unable to believe what they just heard.

00:20:57.550 --> 00:20:59.380
But in the coming moment,

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:04.370
every person in that room 
would fear Akagi.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:19.150
Next time, "The Path of the Storm."

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>The Path of the Storm</b>
